{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00488 - MONDO_3582",
  "verbalization": "Altretamine is linked to Hereditary Breast Ovarian Cancer Syndrome through a series of indications that suggest a potential role in the development of this condition. The evidence indicates that Altretamine is associated with Malignant Non-dysgerminomatous Germ Cell Tumor Of Ovary and Ovarian Adenocarcinoma, both of which are linked to Rucaparib, a drug that is indicated for Hereditary Breast Ovarian Cancer Syndrome. This creates a chain of indications that suggests a possible mechanistic connection between Altretamine and the syndrome. The presence of multiple pathways involving Rucaparib, which is known to target BRCA mutations, supports the idea that Altretamine may influence the progression or risk of Hereditary Breast Ovarian Cancer Syndrome through a mechanism involving tumor biology. The integration of these pathways highlights the potential for Altretamine to be a candidate for repurposing in the treatment of this syndrome, though further research is needed to establish a definitive causal relationship.",
